{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:QOU.Knot.JetGradeLengthShift","lean:module:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L262-L275","doc":"**The bond factor.** A bridge is: promote by the fresh generator, then add\n`d` times the original. Its grade generating function is `(X + C d)` times the\noriginal's -- the interface factor, with the `X` coming from Hecke\nmultiplication and the `C d` from the interface scalar.\n\n`GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_bonds` then multiplies these across a list of\nbonds. What that composition still does NOT supply is the per-nucleon\nfactorisation `G_1(x)^A` of the measured composition law; that is the block\nfactorisation, a separate fact, not proved anywhere here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_mulGen_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_mulGen_top","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L254-L260","doc":"Promotion, on the element: multiplying by the fresh generator multiplies the\ngrade generating function by `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_smul","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L247-L252","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_add","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L244-L245","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_eq_gf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf_eq_gf","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L241-L242","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gfOf","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L237-L239","doc":"The grade generating function of an element, read off its own support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_top","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L215-L224","doc":"The relation on a general element, by linearity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_single_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_single_top","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L203-L213","doc":"**The Hecke relation at the fresh top generator, with nothing assumed.**\n`JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop_ne` discharges the hypothesis for *every*\npermutation -- the length always moves, rising by one when `(sub, top)` was not\nan inversion and falling by one when it was.\n\nThis is what stops `mulGen_mulGen_single` being a vacuous statement about an\nunsatisfiable hypothesis: at `sTop` the hypothesis is a theorem, for all `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_mulGen_single","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L180-L200","doc":"**The Hecke relation.** Applying the rule twice gives `A ·(once) + (id)`,\nwhich is `T_s² = A·T_s + 1` read on the basis element `T_w`.\n\nThe hypothesis `hne` is the real content and is not decoration. If the length\nwere allowed to stay put under `s`, the descending branch would be taken twice\nand the relation would fail outright -- so this theorem is a genuine constraint\non `s`, satisfied by a simple reflection (where the length parity flips) and not\nby an arbitrary permutation. Stating it for arbitrary `s` without `hne` would be\nfalse, which is precisely why it is worth proving rather than assuming. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_single","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L176-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_add","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L171-L174","doc":"`mulGen` really is linear, not merely described as such. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm_add","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L166-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm_zero","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gf_mulGen_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gf_mulGen_top","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L138-L152","doc":"**The join at the fresh top generator**, with the length hypothesis\ndischarged by `JetGradeLengthShift.length_mul_sTop` rather than assumed. For an\nelement supported on permutations that fix the top point -- i.e. one embedded\nfrom `H_{n+1}` into `H_{n+2}` -- multiplying by the new generator multiplies the\ngrade generating function by `X`.\n\nThis is the promotion observation of `computations/jet_history_retention_probe.py`\nas a theorem about algebra elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gf_mulGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.gf_mulGen","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L120-L136","doc":"**The join, in general form.** The grade generating function of the product\nis `X` times that of the original, whenever the length rises across the support.\n\nThis is the step `GradedGeneratingFunction.gf_shift` proved for an abstract\nshifted degree function; here the shift comes from Hecke multiplication rather\nthan being assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_support","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L113-L118","doc":"The support of the product is the relabelled support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_apply_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_apply_mul","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L104-L111","doc":"**Coefficient transport.** The product's coefficient at `w · s` is the\noriginal's coefficient at `w` -- the \"every coefficient preserved\" half of the\npromotion observation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mul_right_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mul_right_inj","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L99-L102","doc":"Right multiplication by a fixed permutation is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_eq_mapDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen_eq_mapDomain","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L88-L97","doc":"**Multiplication is relabelling when the length rises.** If every element of\nthe support ascends under `s`, the splitting branch is never taken, so the whole\nproduct is `Finsupp.mapDomain` along `(· * s)`: every coefficient carried across\nto a new index, nothing split and nothing collapsed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.mulGen","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L84-L86","doc":"Right multiplication by the generator `T_s`, extended linearly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.genTerm","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L77-L82","doc":"The Hecke right-action rule applied to a single term `c * T_w`, with Hecke\nparameter `A = q - q⁻¹`. The second branch is the one that splits a term across\ntwo filtration grades. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.Tw","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L74-L75","doc":"The basis element `T_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.Hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.HeckeTwBasis.Hecke","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/HeckeTwBasis.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The `T_w` basis carrier: finitely-supported `R`-combinations of the `n!`\npermutations. This is the free module on `{T_w : w}` and nothing more; the\nalgebra structure is not built here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}